-- Opens files, transfers their contents, creates directories, and joins paths.
use io as streams.
public use "fs" function open(path text, mode text) giving fallible pointer to streams.Stream.
public use "fs" function read(path text) giving fallible text.
public use "fs" function write(path text, content text) giving fallible nothing.
public use "fs" function directory(path text) giving fallible nothing.
public use "fs" function join(left text, right text) giving fallible text.
-- Advanced stream controls. Offsets are byte offsets; origin is start, current, or end.
public use "fs" function flush(stream pointer to streams.Stream) giving fallible nothing.
public use "fs" function seek(stream pointer to streams.Stream, offset integer 64, origin text) giving fallible nothing.
public use "fs" function position(stream pointer to streams.Stream) giving fallible unsigned 64.
public use "fs" function size(stream pointer to streams.Stream) giving fallible unsigned 64.
